[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536470726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112778#issuecomment-3536470726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112778","id":3536470726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SykLG","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T13:06:04Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T13:06:04Z","body":"Can confirm in `v4.5.1.stable`, but not on `v4.6.dev4`, where it appears to be fixed. Can you please confirm on the latest dev build?\n\n **v4.5.1.stable**\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa1be585-0e34-407c-bed7-b7404c3b79d6\n\n**v4.6.dev4**\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0138bbcc-42d2-440c-9922-0eb2f5027e92","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536470726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536800894","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112778#issuecomment-3536800894","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112778","id":3536800894,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sz0x-","user":{"login":"zommerfelds","id":1260622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjA2MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1260622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds","html_url":"https://github.com/zommerfelds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T19:23:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T19:25:22Z","body":"I just tested on `Godot v4.6.dev4 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Intel Corporation; 32.0.101.6737) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1185G7 @ 3.00GHz (8 threads) - 15.83 GiB memory`\n\nThe behavior is still not right:\n\n<img width=\"1316\" height=\"1143\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f63795d-f5c8-4f38-8b05-67d9530048c9\" />\n\nThe heighmap is just a solid block, it's not taking the shape into account (4.5.1 on Mac was the opposite, there was no collision at all). If I switch to Forward+ and Compatibility it's still fine.\n\nNote that on @rsubtil's first video it's actually half working, just some blocks are clipping through. With me everything is falling through on the current stable version.\n\nI can test v4.6.dev4 on Mac too later.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536800894/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3540100679","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112778#issuecomment-3540100679","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112778","id":3540100679,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TAaZH","user":{"login":"zommerfelds","id":1260622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjA2MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1260622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds","html_url":"https://github.com/zommerfelds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zommerfelds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T05:55:47Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T05:55:47Z","body":"OK sorry I won't be able to test in on MacOS (it's not my computer and I can't install other versions). But at least we know that it's reproducible on my Windows machine.\nOne more input though: it seems like on Android the behavior is yet different again: even with Compatibility mode the particle collisions are not working. So it seems like the behavior is quite system dependent :/","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3540100679/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3545520588","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112778#issuecomment-3545520588","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112778","id":3545520588,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TVFnM","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T06:28:22Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T06:28:22Z","body":"I can repro the issue on MacOS. I wonder if it is due to the missing depth resolve described here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/78598#issuecomment-3492314163\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108636 added a depth resolve in dev1. But it sounds like that form of automatic depth resolve doesn't work with Metal on Apple devices. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3545520588/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3555548762","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112778#issuecomment-3555548762","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112778","id":3555548762,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7T7V5a","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T02:55:29Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T02:55:29Z","body":"> [#108636](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108636) added a depth resolve in dev1. But it sounds like that form of automatic depth resolve doesn't work with Metal on Apple devices.\n\nI think that's because that solution resolve to the depth backbuffer, not to the normal depth buffer.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3555548762/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6030432509","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112778#issuecomment-6030432509","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112778","id":6030432509,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZ3EY_Q","user":{"login":"Cr3sta","id":95083342,"node_id":"U_kgDOBarbTg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95083342?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta","html_url":"https://github.com/Cr3sta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-07T03:41:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T03:41:59Z","body":"I think I found (at least one) root cause of the Mobile-only behaviour, details in #124252.\n\nIn `RenderForwardMobile::_render_particle_collider_heightfield()` (`servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp`) the heightfield depth pass is drawn with `_render_list_with_draw_list(&render_list_params, p_fb);` i.e. with the default draw flags, so the heightfield depth texture is **loaded** instead of cleared. Forward+ passes `RD::DRAW_CLEAR_ALL` in the same place, and 4.3 Mobile used `INITIAL_ACTION_CLEAR` (lost in the DrawFlags refactor).\n\nConsequences:\n- The depth test keeps the highest value, so every update only *adds* to the old contents. A heightfield that is moved (follow camera, or simply repositioned, including in the editor) becomes a \"solid block\" at the highest height it has ever seen — which matches the 4.6.dev4 Windows/Vulkan report above.\n- A freshly created heightfield texture starts with whatever was in that memory: it is not cleared on creation on Vulkan (only D3D12 sets `API_TRAIT_TEXTURE_OUTPUTS_REQUIRE_CLEARS`), so depending on the driver/allocator you can get no collision at all or garbage.\n\nReproduced on 4.7.2.stable / Windows 11 / Vulkan / NVIDIA, with MSAA disabled (the heightfield framebuffer is single-sampled anyway, so depth resolve should not be involved). Passing `RD::DRAW_CLEAR_ALL` there (the Mobile `_render_list_with_draw_list` already defaults the depth clear value to 0.0 = far with reversed-Z) should fix it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6030432509/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6030493731","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112778#issuecomment-6030493731","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112778","id":6030493731,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZ3IIIw","user":{"login":"Cr3sta","id":95083342,"node_id":"U_kgDOBarbTg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95083342?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta","html_url":"https://github.com/Cr3sta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cr3sta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-07T03:47:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T03:47:11Z","body":"One more data point: this was already fixed once for 4.4 in #102133 (\"Fix framebuffer clear for particle collider heightfield\", fixes #100793) — but that one-line patch only touched `render_forward_clustered.cpp`. The Mobile counterpart in `render_forward_mobile.cpp` never got the `RD::DRAW_CLEAR_ALL`, so Mobile still has the bug that Forward+ had in 4.4dev6/dev7. Details and a repro in #124252.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6030493731/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]